# Build context. Anything here is invisible to `docker build`, which is also
# what CI builds from — and CI checks out only *tracked* files, so every
# local-only path in .gitignore has to be repeated here or it leaks in.
#
# That repetition is the whole reason this file exists beyond size: without
# it, a developer's `docker build --target checks` lints files CI will never
# see. It is not hypothetical — `.claude/worktrees/<name>/` is an untracked
# git worktree, and because the patterns below are ROOT-ANCHORED (Docker
# matches them against the full path), a bare `tests` excludes only the
# top-level `tests/` and not a worktree's own copy of one. So a stray
# worktree arrived in the context with its tests, src and configs, and the
# `checks` stage reported eight lint warnings against files that do not
# exist in CI's checkout. Real lint signal was 1 of 9.

node_modules
.next
.git
.env
.env.local
docs
*.md
tests
vitest.config.ts

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Mirrors .gitignore. `docker-compose.override.yml` is the local-only
# Compose override, and .rebuild-state is scripts/rebuild.sh's saved
# change-detection state — neither belongs in an image, and the second is
# specific to whichever box is deploying.
docker-compose.override.yml
.rebuild-state
*.tsbuildinfo

# Agent/editor tooling. `.claude/launch.json` is tracked, but the worktrees
# nested inside it are not, and they are whole checkouts of the repo.
.claude